<article class="prose experience">
  <h1>What it feels like to use</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The technology is invisible by design. Here's what each person actually
    does — and what they no longer have to.
  </p>

  <h2>The story, end to end</h2>
  <ol class="journey">
    <li>
      <h3>The university issues a diploma</h3>
      <p>
        A graduate clicks <em>"Add to wallet"</em> on the university portal — or
        scans a QR code at the ceremony. They pick the wallet app they already
        use. The diploma lands in it in seconds.
      </p>
      <p class="aside">No new account. No vendor the university chose for them.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>The graduate holds it</h3>
      <p>
        The diploma now lives in the graduate's wallet, on their phone, under
        their control — like a boarding pass or a payment card. It works even if
        the university's website is down years later.
      </p>
      <p class="aside">They can move it to a different wallet whenever they like.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>An admissions office verifies it</h3>
      <p>
        The graduate applies to a master's program abroad. The application page
        asks for proof of their degree. They tap <em>"Share diploma"</em>,
        approve once, and the admissions office confirms it instantly —
        cryptographically, no phone calls to the registrar.
      </p>
      <p class="aside">Verified in seconds, across borders, in any language.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What the graduate experiences</h2>
  <ul class="benefits">
    <li><strong>Three taps, not three weeks.</strong> Receive, hold, share.</li>
    <li><strong>Their choice of wallet.</strong> Not dictated by the school or a government list.</li>
    <li><strong>They stay in control.</strong> Nothing is shared without an explicit, one-time approval.</li>
    <li><strong>It keeps working.</strong> The credential doesn't depend on the issuer staying online.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What the institution experiences</h2>
  <ul class="benefits">
    <li><strong>No identity silo to run.</strong> You issue a credential; you don't host the user's login.</li>
    <li><strong>Instant, tamper-evident verification.</strong> No manual transcript checks.</li>
    <li><strong>No vendor lock-in.</strong> Pick a provider, swap it later, keep working with every wallet.</li>
    <li><strong>Cross-border by default.</strong> A diploma issued here verifies anywhere that reads the standard.</li>
  </ul>

